  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Frozen a deterministic 100-field cubic LMFDB corpus with 10 smoke, 60 tuning, and 30 held-out records, exact selection/source/content hashes, pinned-label replay, and offline validation. Added a strict v3 four-boundary evidence receipt and Sage.js, Sage/PARI, and direct-GP runners. Receipts bind requested versus achieved proof semantics, a common regulator-accuracy contract, exact rounded-decimal uncertainty, every retained sample answer/proof, streamed independent-field microbatches, phase timing, explicitly scoped process peak RSS, source/host/tool identity, resolved dynamic math libraries, and generated Sage.js runtime/native artifacts. Timing and per-operation memory eligibility are independent fail-closed decisions.",
    "risks": [
      "Magma, Hecke, and Oscar are inventoried when available, but their corpus execution adapters remain explicitly unsupported. The 2026-08-25 local dry-run found Magma 2.18-5, Hecke 0.40.0, and Oscar 1.9.0-DEV; availability is host-specific.",
      "No packaged Sage.js release launcher is provisioned, so release-cold Sage.js remains explicitly unavailable.",
      "Source Sage.js evidence intentionally remains unavailable until a build receipt and ignored runtime/native artifact trees exactly match the clean benchmark revision.",
      "Persistent case-process peak RSS is explicitly memory-ineligible for Gate C; a dedicated single-operation memory run is still required.",
      "Exact timed execution currently requires GNU time and timeout on Linux; native process/RSS supervisors remain to be implemented for Windows and macOS.",
      "The pinned stratified snapshot covers cubic smoke/tune/holdout workloads only; higher degrees and large-discriminant stress corpora remain future laboratory work."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Implement direct Magma and Julia Hecke/Oscar adapters with the same proof, output, regulator, batch, RSS, and artifact-identity contract.",
      "Build Sage.js at the exact integrated clean revision, run smoke plus tuning on this host and bench-1, freeze optimization choices, and only then observe the held-out tier.",
      "Provision and fingerprint the packaged Sage.js release for release-cold measurements.",
      "Add native process-group and RSS supervisors for Windows and macOS before accepting performance evidence on those hosts.",
      "Extend pinned corpora to degrees 2 through 10 and add large-memory/verification stress tiers before claiming broad Gate performance."
    ]
  }
